From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 11:20:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 367/638] [AROS] Prove Mojo invitations between Processes

AI_PHASE: chromium-process-model
AI_STATUS: cross-process-invitation-runtime-pass
ROOT_CAUSE: Raw Channel traffic was proven across AROS Processes, but Chromium's real NodeController invitation and primordial-pipe bootstrap remained unverified.
FIX_REASON: Add a focused AROS-only parent/child probe using LaunchProcess, OutgoingInvitation, IncomingInvitation, independent IO workers, named primordial pipe traffic, and native DOS termination after Mojo cleanup.
SCOPE: mojo/core/BUILD.gn; mojo/core/invitation_aros_process_probe.cc
VALIDATION: Hosted 16 GiB run reported child PASS, parent PASS invitation=1 primordial=2, collected child death, restored startup, and exited zero in 8.11 seconds.
RISK: The probe uses FAST Mojo shutdown and records an unclean-node warning; browser/renderer roles must next prove their production lifecycle and service binding.
AI_DECISION_CHAIN: direct Channel PASS -> full invitation -> primordial request/reply -> stdc threaded exit stall -> native DOS Exit after IO stop -> clean guest exit.
Evidence:-invitation-aros-process-20260728
Job:
---
 mojo/core/BUILD.gn                         |  11 ++
 mojo/core/invitation_aros_process_probe.cc | 190 +++++++++++++++++++++
